{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081517Z_dev-03_flat_59b5", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the ψψ̄ → h2h2 channel, the best fit in Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089) has m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. The annihilation cross section is ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹, with Ωh² = 0.121. The canonical J-factor was rescaled by 𝒥 = 2.2, meaning J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical. This gives χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}]}, "turns": 3, "seconds": 8.489, "tool_calls": 2, "tool_result_chars": 51248, "input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 608, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 26079, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5308, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:15:26+00:00"}
